  "notes": "Compound of {点|てん} (point/check) + {呼|こ} (call). The act of calling names or numbers to verify attendance.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {点呼|てんこ}をとる: to take roll call\n- {点呼|てんこ}する: to do a roll call\n- {点呼|てんこ}を{行|おこな}う: to conduct a roll call (formal)\n- {朝|あさ}の{点呼|てんこ}: morning roll call\n\nUSAGE:\nUsed in settings where attendance verification is important:\n- {軍隊|ぐんたい}: military\n- {学校|がっこう}: school (especially field trips, evacuations)\n- {避難|ひなん}{訓練|くんれん}: evacuation drills\n- {工事|こうじ}{現場|げんば}: construction sites\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {出欠|しゅっけつ}をとる: to take attendance (classroom setting, more everyday)\n- {人数|にんずう}{確認|かくにん}: headcount/confirmation of numbers",
